  "provider_query": "The first YouTube video, Me at the zoo",
  "answer": "**“Me at the zoo” is the first video uploaded to YouTube.**\n\n- **Uploader and date:** YouTube co-founder Jawed Karim posted it on April 23, 2005 (around 8:27 p.m. PDT), on the channel “jawed.” It remains his only upload.  \n  Sources: [Wikipedia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Me_at_the_zoo), [Jawed Karim – Wikipedia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jawed_Karim)\n\n- **Content:** A roughly 19-second clip filmed by high-school friend Yakov Lapitsky at the San Diego Zoo. Karim stands in front of elephants and says they have “really, really, really long trunks, and that’s cool.”  \n  Sources: [Wikipedia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Me_at_the_zoo), [Wikitubia](https://youtube.fandom.com/wiki/Me_at_the_zoo)\n\n- **Original video:** [youtube.com/watch?v=jNQXAC9IVRw](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=jNQXAC9IVRw) — hundreds of millions of views (reports in 2025–2026 range from about 350 million to over 440 million).  \n  Sources: [YouTube listing](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=jNQXAC9IVRw), [Tubefilter (Apr 2025)](https://www.tubefilter.com/2025/04/23/20-years-youtube-me-at-the-zoo-2005-jawed-karim/)\n\n- **Significance:** Often called YouTube’s first vlog and a milestone of user-generated video. It tested the new site’s simple upload-and-play model.  \n  Sources: [Tubefilter](https://www.tubefilter.com/2025/04/23/20-years-youtube-me-at-the-zoo-2005-jawed-karim/), [Apple Scoop](https://applescoop.org/story/history-of-youtube-me-at-the-zoo-to-tv-giant)\n\n- **Zoo reaction:** The official San Diego Zoo channel left a pinned comment in 2020 (“We’re so honored…”) that became one of the most-liked comments on YouTube.  \n  Sources: [Wikipedia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Me_at_the_zoo), [Wikitubia](https://youtube.fandom.com/wiki/Me_at_the_zoo)\n\n- **Later notes:** Karim has occasionally changed the description to comment on YouTube policy (e.g., Google+ comments, dislike counts).  \n  Sources: [The Sun (Apr 2025)](https://www.the-sun.com/tech/14087057/youtube-first-video-me-at-the-zoo-google-karim/), [Wikitubia](https://youtube.fandom.com/wiki/Me_at_the_zoo)\n\n- **Background:** Karim, Steve Chen, and Chad Hurley (ex-PayPal) registered the domain in February 2005; Google bought YouTube in 2006 for $1.65 billion.  \n  Sources: [Apple Scoop](https://applescoop.org/story/history-of-youtube-me-at-the-zoo-to-tv-giant), [Jawed Karim – Wikipedia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jawed_Karim)\n\n- **Explainer video:** EmpLemon’s “Me at the zoo | YouTube Geographic” covers the clip’s history and context.  \n  Source: [YouTube](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=dcZY3yi8Xbw)",
